4. What Was Kept, Changed, and Verified
•	Gantt chart: Kept the original single-chart presentation approach while expanding the schedule and adding a brief overall description.
•	Trello: Kept the existing product backlog and two sprint lists; added proposed task ownership, deadlines, and screenshot documentation. Planned development tasks were not represented as completed.
•	Risk register: Kept the original 16 entries and added proposed technical security risk TR5 and schedule risk SR5, bringing the proposed total to 18.
•	Quality, communications, stakeholders, budget, and RACI: Reviewed the existing sections and generally retained them instead of rewriting material without a demonstrated need.
•	Project closure: Preserved the distinction between completed planning work and unexecuted implementation, testing, and deployment. Recommended consistency edits to dates and risk counts.
•	Maintenance proposal: Retained the proposed hybrid contract and financial framework; clarified the 17-month combined build-plus-maintenance period, SLA language, and proposed rather than executed status.
•	Video deliverable: Kept the original closure video link and identified the new assignment video as a separate update highlighting recent changes.
5. Student Review and Responsibility
The project owner reviewed AI-generated recommendations, chose which revisions to adopt, and updated the project materials and Trello board. Proposed assignments, deadlines, costs, and SLAs should be understood as planning assumptions unless independently validated. This disclosure does not claim that software implementation or live testing occurred.

